{
  "result": "If I had one magic lever to pull, it wouldn't be to make everyone rich or perfectly happy \u2014 I think people find meaning in striving, in struggle, in figuring things out for themselves.\n\nI'd pull this one: **Make sure where you're born doesn't decide how your life turns out.**\n\nRight now, so much human potential is just wasted by accident of birth \u2014 no clean water, no school, no doctor, no safety, no one to believe in you. Not because those people lack talent or work ethic, but because they never got a baseline to start from.\n\nIf I could give everyone that baseline \u2014 enough food and shelter you don't have to worry about, healthcare when you're sick, an education that actually opens doors, and just the basic security that the world isn't actively against you \u2014 then people could finally choose their own paths. Fail, try again, become weird, become kind, become brilliant, whatever *they* want.\n\nNot utopia. Just a fair starting line.\n\nWhat about you? If you got to pull the lever, what would you change?",
